        "Categories": {
          "value": "SVG flags with an aspect ratio of 3:2|With insignia|Self-published work|PD-self|SVG flags of the European Union|Valid SVG created with Text Editor:Flags",
          "source": "commons-categories",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "Assessments": {
          "value": "",
          "source": "commons-categories",
          "hidden": ""
        },
        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flag_of_Europe\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Flag of Europe\">Flag of Europe</a> is the flag and emblem of the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/European_Union\" title=\"European Union\">European Union</a> (EU) and <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Europe\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Council of Europe\">Council of Europe</a> (CoE). It consists of a circle of 12 <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Gold\" title=\"Gold\">golden</a> (<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Yellow\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Yellow\">yellow</a>) stars on a <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Blue\" title=\"Blue\">blue</a> background. It was created in 1955 by the CoE and adopted by the EU, then the European Communities, in the 1980s.\n<p>The CoE and EU are distinct in membership and nature. The CoE is an international organisation with 46 members, dealing with human rights and rule of law, while the EU is a quasi-federal union of 27 states, focused on economic integration and political cooperation. Today, the flag is mostly associated with the latter.\n</p>\nIt was the intention of the CoE that the flag should come to represent <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Europe\" title=\"Europe\">Europe</a> as a whole, and since its adoption the membership of the CoE covers nearly the entire Europe by the number of states involved, although only a little over half of the European continent by territory. This is why the EU adopted the same flag. The flag has been used to represent Europe in sporting events and as a pro-democracy banner outside the European Union.",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
        "Credit": {
          "value": "<ul><li>File created by various Wikimedia users (see \"Author\").</li>\n<li>File based on the specification given at <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://europa.eu/abc/symbols/emblem/graphics1_en.htm\">[1]</a>.</li></ul>",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
